  <h2 id="hot-take" class="scroll-mt-20">My design hot take: This is about change adoption</h2>
  <p>All the focus on AI's technological advancement missed a critical aspect: employee adoption. An agentic process will disrupt how the team has always worked. Before we could even debate whether a proposal was good, a few conditions had to be true:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>PMs are motivated to visit the portal.</li>
    <li>Proposals are relevant and actionable.</li>
    <li>Proposals are easy to digest and quick to review.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="workshop" class="scroll-mt-20">Service design workshop</h2>
  <p><strong>How do we create those conditions?</strong></p>
  <p>I facilitated one-hour workshops with four principal PMs. Using journey mapping, we traced each stage of product development: what PMs do, how they do it, and where the biggest joys and pain points are. We closed with a future-state review to understand their mindset about AI and change.</p>
  <p class="text-gray-400 italic">Results are coming soon — stay tuned!</p>
